# Marketplace layout — client-approved, do not change silently

The client signed off on these layouts and has asked twice for them to be
restored after they were changed. Treat them as requirements, not preferences.
If a change seems visually better, propose it first — do not just apply it.

## Offer and category lists show two cards per row on phones

Every offer/product list must fit **two cards per row below `sm` (640px)**.
Category preview rows use a 2-column grid on phones and only become a
horizontal swipe row from `sm` up.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — fixed-width cards in a flex row: ~1.5 cards fit a 360px phone,
//          so it reads as one per row with sideways scrolling.
<div className="flex overflow-x-auto gap-5">
  <div className="min-w-[220px] w-[240px] flex-shrink-0">…</div>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — two per row on phones, swipe row from sm up.
<div className="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:flex sm:gap-5 sm:overflow-x-auto">
  <div className="w-full min-w-0 sm:min-w-[220px] sm:w-[240px] sm:flex-shrink-0">…</div>
</div>
```

Applies to `AtiStore.tsx` and the `variant="ati"` branch of
`OfferCardSkeleton.tsx` — the skeleton must match the real grid or the layout
visibly jumps from one-up to two-up while loading.

Never drop the base `grid-cols-2` to `grid-cols-1`, and never reintroduce a
mobile `min-w-[...]`/`w-[...]` on a card that sits in these rows.

**Exception — `ProducerMarket.tsx` (2026-08-03):** the collapsed category row,
Recommended row, and `variant="producer"` skeleton were deliberately switched to
an unconditional horizontal-scroll row on explicit client request, to match the
homepage carousel. This is intentional — the "BAD" pattern above is what was
applied here on purpose, but with the mobile card narrowed to `w-40`
(`min-w-[250px]`) instead of ~220-260px, so ~2 cards stay visible on a 360px
phone instead of ~1.5. Do not revert this to a grid without re-confirming with
the client — see `docs/UI-LAYOUT-RULES.md` §1 for the full explanation.

## Card text must fit a half-width phone card

Two per row leaves roughly 150px of usable card width, so card typography has to
scale down on phones or it wraps and collides:

- Price is `text-sm`/`text-base` on phones, `md:text-lg` up. Never `text-lg` at
  the base — `12,321 FCFA (XAF)` does not fit on one line.
- Never put two columns side by side in the card footer at the base width, and
  never mark one of them `shrink-0` there: it starves the other, which is what
  wrapped the price onto three lines on top of the stock figure. Stack with
  `flex-col` and switch to `sm:flex-row`.
- Give unit/label lines `min-w-0` plus `truncate` so long unit names cannot push
  the layout wider.

## The chat composer must stay reachable

In `SupportChatWidget.tsx` the panel is fixed-height with `overflow-hidden`, so
any block that can grow will push the send button past the bottom edge:

- Keep `flex-1 min-h-0` on the message list.
- Keep the guest form capped and scrollable (`max-h-[70%] overflow-y-auto`).
- Keep the effect that re-clamps a dragged position on resize,
  `orientationchange`, `visualViewport` resize, and `ResizeObserver`.

